L001261	\subsection{3D $d$-wave altermagnet: La$_2$NiO$_4$}
L001262	\label{subsec:La2NiO4}
L001263	
L001264	La$_2$NiO$_4$ is a Ruddlesden-Popper compound with parent space group $I4/mmm$~\cite{rodriguez-carvajalNeutronDiffractionStudy1991}. Symmetry-mode analysis indicates concomitant antiferroaxial and antiferromagnetic instabilities at the $X$ point $\mathbf{q}=(\pi,\pi,0)$, yielding $G_{110}\sim X_3^+$ and $\mathbf{N}\sim X_1^+$. Their bilinear combination transforms as
L001265	\begin{equation}
L001266	G_{110}\mathbf{N}\sim X_3^+\otimes X_1^+ = \Gamma_5^+(E_g),
L001267	\end{equation}
L001268	which couples to the $E_g$ channel of the rank $\ell=2$ magnetic multipole, indicating a $d$-wave altermagnetic state. Upon condensation, $G_{110}$ lowers the crystallographic symmetry to $I4_2/ncm$, and the N\'{e}el order further reduces it to the space group $Pccn$ (point group $mmm$), in which the N\'{e}el order transforms as $\Gamma_3^+$, consistent with the $d_{xy}$-wave altermagnetic spin splitting shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:La2NiO4}(c).
L001269	
L001270	\textit{Computational details:} We used $U=6$ eV for atom Ni and a $9\times 9\times 4$ k mesh (cutoff 550 eV).
